<title>PORTUGAL: Portucel raising pulp prices from May 1.</title>
<headline>Portucel raising pulp prices from May 1.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese pulp producer Portucel Industrial said on Monday that it was raising pulp prices to 450 ecu per tonne from 400 ecu previously with effect from May 1.  </p>
<p>A company spokesman said that the increase was justified by the significant improvement in market conditions and because the last increase on April 1 had been easily absorbed.</p>
<p>Some Nordic producers have also announced price increases.</p>
<p>Portucel officials were making a presentation to analysts in London on Monday and Tuesday. On April 28 and 29, similar presentations will be held in New York and Boston.</p>
<p>--Jose Barata, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
</text>
